  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Security and Rural Development - Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smallholders (men and women) have increased income and access to markets. The project will contribute to increase smallholders&#x2019; production and profits by training them on product transformation,  promoting  participation  in  local  markets  with  fair  trade,  and  short marketing circuits. Capacity building in best fish farming practices, access to private and self-management  funds  will  also  be  delivered. Support  families  to  obtain &quot;sustainable seals&quot; meaning that the coffe was produced in an environmentally sustainable manner. It will give them access to premium prices and differentiated markets for specialty coffee. Relevant activities include: commercialization of production in local markets; access to public/private credits; access to premium prices for sustainable specialty coffee; and artisanal fishing families improve their marketing chain. Special attention will be given to the participation of women, youth and persons living with disabilities (PLWD).</narrative>
  </description>
